From 246762de38a6e4617a9ec60afe742f883d2de6f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:42:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 34/35] vendor: port github.com/ishidawataru/sctp to FreeBSD
 (agnhost SCTP)

agnhost's SCTP client/server (porter, netexec, connect) use this library,
whose only implementation was Linux's; on FreeBSD every call returned
"SCTP is unsupported on freebsd/arm64", so no SCTP e2e test could run.

FreeBSD has a native SCTP stack with the same one-to-one socket API, but
different option numbers, flags, struct sizes and sockaddrs with sa_len:

- Linux's option/flag/cmsg constants and address handling move from
  sctp.go to sctp_os_other.go (!freebsd), unchanged.
- sctp_freebsd.go: FreeBSD values; bind(2) then SCTP_BINDX_ADD_ADDR (one
  bare sockaddr per call); connect(2), or SCTP_CONNECT_X for several
  addresses; SCTP_GET_{LOCAL,PEER}_ADDRESSES parsed by sa_len; 128-byte
  sctp_sndrcvinfo cmsgs; SCTP_EVENTS / SCTP_DEFAULT_SEND_PARAM widened from
  the Linux-sized structs; EOF = empty non-notification read (FreeBSD
  attaches a zeroed SNDRCV cmsg at EOF); GetStatus, primary peer address
  and PeelOff return ErrUnsupported.
- ipsock_linux.go -> ipsock_unix.go (linux || freebsd);
  sctp_unsupported.go no longer builds on freebsd.

Checked on FreeBSD 15.1 arm64: multi-homed listen/dial, SNDRCV info both
ways, events, default send params, addresses, EOF, refused.
